TEXT 408 152 Left 2 ;An open delta connection transformer uses two single-phase\ntransformer to supply a three phase load. Also known as a V-V\nsystem, this setup is typically used only in emergencies \n(one transformer in revision or disconnected for repair)\nbecause it is less efficient than a closed delta. (factor 1.73205)\nThis combination can supply a maximum of 17.32kVA\nwhereas each transformer operates at its rated capacity\nat 10KVA
TEXT 144 192 Left 2 ;See Q is flowing in circle\nfrom trafo1 to trafo2 and \nreturn (only inside)
TEXT 152 464 Left 2 ;This is a normal transformer with 3x1 transormers\noperating at nominal power
TEXT 144 72 Left 2 ;10<0°A
TEXT 208 152 Left 2 ;10<-120°A
TEXT 152 232 Left 2 ;10<120°A
TEXT 216 120 Left 2 ;1k<30°V
TEXT 264 200 Left 2 ;1k<90°V
TEXT 408 248 Left 2 ;From picture above you can see that\nFrom Transformer1 S=U*conj(I)=1000<30° * conj(-10<0°) = -8660.2-j5000 \n(Transformer1 delivers active power 8660W and also delivers\n reactive power 5000VAr to the second transformer)\nFrom Transformer2 S=U*conj(I)=1000<90° * conj(-10<120°) = -8660.2+j5000\n(Transformer2 delivers active power to port2 and consumes\nreactive power from transformer1\nYou can see that active load of both transformers is 8660W and\nand there is an exchange of reacitve power between transformer1\nand transformer2 !!\nDue to this reason total kVA rating of transformers\nis more than kVA rating of the load !!!!!\nSqrt(8660*8660+5000*5000)=10kVA is the rating of the transformers
TEXT -8 88 Left 1 ;NOTE reactive power\nflow positive in the\ndirection of the \nsmall arrow symbol
TEXT 88 24 Left 2 !.ac list 49.99 50 50.01
TEXT 408 104 Left 2 !.meas AC Qflow12 PARAM V(N003,N001)*Ix(U1:s1)\n.meas AC Qflow21 PARAM V(N006,N003)*-Ix(U2:s1)
